            "text": "{\"primary_meaning\":\"Sin, spiritual blindness, evil, death, and separation from God, often representing the domain of Satan in contrast to the light of God.\",\"primary_basis\":[\"John 1:5\",\"John 3:19\",\"1 John 1:5-6\",\"Ephesians 5:8-11\",\"Colossians 1:13\"],\"alternatives\":[{\"meaning\":\"Divine mystery, transcendence, and the unsearchable presence of God, often referred to as divine darkness or thick cloud.\",\"basis\":[\"Exodus 20:21\",\"1 Kings 8:12\",\"Psalm 18:11\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"},{\"meaning\":\"Divine judgment, eschatological wrath, affliction, and eternal punishment, such as outer darkness.\",\"basis\":[\"Amos 5:18-20\",\"Zephaniah 1:15\",\"Matthew 8:12\",\"Jude 1:13\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"},{\"meaning\":\"Natural ignorance or a lack of divine revelation prior to the coming of Christ.\",\"basis\":[\"Isaiah 9:2\",\"Matthew 4:16\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"}],\"has_settled_consensus\":true,\"confidence\":\"high\",\"notes\":\"While darkness predominantly symbolizes evil, sin, and judgment in Christian theology, there is a well-established secondary tradition regarding the divine darkness of God's incomprehensibility and hiddenness, drawn primarily from Old Testament theophanies.\"}",
